    <DataNode elementId="AT1G01290-MONOMER" textLabel="AT1G01290-MONOMER" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q39056" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="300" centerY="355" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="THE-ARABIDOPSIS-INFORMATION-RESOURCE, hartmut">The cDNA encoding a protein involved in the early steps of molybdenum cofactor biosynthesis (Cnx3) has been isolated from &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana&lt;/i&gt;. The Cnx3, together with a second protein (Cnx2) was able to rescue &lt;i&gt;E. coli&lt;/i&gt; mutants that have been unable to grow on nitrogen medium under anaerobic conditions because of lacking nitrate reductase activity |CITS: [7890743]|. It has been found that Cnx3 has strong sequence similarity to the &lt;i&gt;E. coli&lt;/i&gt; gene moaC that is known to be involved in the early steps of the molybdenum cofactor biosynthesis in this bacterium |CITS: [8514782]|. Cnx3 is weakly expressed in all tissues, the strongest expression is observed in the roots of Arabidopsis. The N-terminal extension found in the enzyme supports a possible location of the enzyme in either chloroplasts or mitochondria.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT1G01290-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT1G01290.1" />
