      <Graphics lineColor="000000" lineStyle="Solid" lineWidth="1.0" connectorType="Straight" />
      <Comment source="BioCyc">A eukaryotic enzyme that transfers sulfur to form a thiocarboxylate moiety on the small subunit of EC 2.8.1.d, molybdopterin synthase. In the human, the reaction is catalysed by the rhodanese-like C-terminal domain of the MOCS3 protein, a bifunctional protein that also contains |FRAME: RXN-11361 &quot;EC 2.7.7.k, molybdopterin-synthase adenylyltransferase&quot;| at the N-terminal domain.</Comment>
