  <Groups>
    <Group elementId="CPLX-7191" textLabel="CPLX-7191" type="Complex">
      <Xref identifier="CPLX-7191" dataSource="plantcyc" />
      <Graphics centerX="300" centerY="275" width="140" height="100" textColor="666666" fontName="Arial" fontSize="10" borderColor="9900CC" borderStyle="Dashed" borderWidth="2.0" fillColor="F5E6FF" shapeType="Rectangle" zOrder="-1" />
      <Comment source="THE-ARABIDOPSIS-INFORMATION-RESOURCE, hartmut">The functional molybdopterin synthase (MTP synthase) is a heterotetramer that consists of 2 large subunits (Cnx6) and 2 small subunits (Cnx7) |CITS: [9421926]| |CITS: [12147719]|. The large subunit Cnx6 was identified based on sequence homology to its bacterial complement MoaE and the small subunit (Cnx7) using a yeast two-hybrid screen |CITS: [11459846]|. The structure and function of the enzyme including the mechanism of the catalyzed reaction has been investigated in detail in bacteria |CITS: [11135669][12571227][12571226]|.</Comment>
